<addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI EIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOYAMA NOBUTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHNOGI HIROMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAGAWA HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKAI, KATSUSHIGE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, IKUNOSHIN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, EIJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOYAMA, NOBUTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHNOGI, HIROMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAGAWA, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>5-Membered ring compounds represented by general formula (I), optically active isomers thereof or salts of the same. These compounds have physiological activities including a carcinostatic effect. In said formula the bond shown by the dotted line in the 5-membered ring represents that this 5-membered ring may be either a cyclopentene ring having a double bond or a saturated cyclopentane ring, and when the 5-membered ring is a cyclopentene ring, X is OR1, Y is =O and Z is H, and when it is a cyclopentane ring, X is =O, Y is OR2 and Z is OR3, (wherein R1 is R4 or -(CO)-R5; R2 is H,-R6 or -(CO)-R7; and R3 is H, R8 or (CO)-R9 (wherein R4, R5, R6, R7, R8 and R9 are the same or different and each represents an aliphatic, aromatic or aliphatic aromatic group, and R5, R7 and R9 may be each H), provided that the case where R2=R3=H is excluded); and W represents a residue obtained by eliminating SH from an SH-containing compound.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des composés cycliques dotés de 5 chaînons, représentés par la formule générale (I), des isomères optiquement actifs ou des sels de ceux-ci. Ces composés possèdent des activités physiologiques, notamment un effet cancérostatique. Dans la formule, la liaison indiquée par la ligne pointillée dans le noyau à 5 chaînons signifie que ce noyau à 5 chaînons peut être un noyau de cyclopentène comportant une liaison double ou un noyau de cyclopentane saturé; lorsque le noyau à 5 chaînons est un noyau de cyclopentène, X est OR1, Y est =O et Z est H, et lorsqu'il est un noyau de cyclopentane, X est =O, Y est OR2 et Z est OR3, (R1 est R4 ou -(CO)-R5; R2 est H, R6 ou -(CO)-R7; et R3 est H, R8 ou -(CO)-R9, (R4, R5, R6, R7, R8 et R9 étant identiques ou différents, et chacun représentant un groupe aliphatique, un groupe aromatique ou un groupe aromatique aliphatique, et R5, R7 et R9 pouvant être chacun H, à condition que le cas où R2=R3=H soit exclu); et W représente un résidu obtenu par élimination de SH d'un composé contenant SH.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>